  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Who gets in",
      "items": [
        "Users are created by an admin only; nobody signs up: backend.ts (allowAdminCreateUserOnly), auth/resource.ts.",
        "An organization (a t-… group of admins) holds workspaces, each with its own ovs-<slug> group; its shared workspace is read by every member (ADR-0024). adminUsers is the one writer of organizations, workspaces and their groups.",
        "An edge signs in with its own app client as its organization's agent; claude.ai through the MCP server, as the person, with the ovs-claude client (ADR-0025). Neither can approve or accept."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Rows",
      "items": [
        "16 models, among them Tenant, Workspace, Story, Decision, Issue, Activity, Connection, LifecycleRun and Artifact: data/resource.ts.",
        "Every row names its workspace's group; members of that group and ovs-admins may reach it. An approval and a story's acceptance are read-only fields only the run function sets."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Objects",
      "items": [
        "workspaces/* in the bucket is open to ovs-admins only: storage/resource.ts. Members go through objectProxy, which checks the workspace's group before it touches a key: functions/objectProxy/handler.ts.",
        "A presigned upload is bound to its SHA-256 and a snapshot is write-once; nothing is deleted through the proxy: functions/shared/uploadPolicy.ts."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Proxy and gate",
      "items": [
        "connections keeps each key in Secrets Manager and only reads: it tests a key and reads Odoo and Shopify for an edge that holds none (ADR-0022).",
        "execute is the one writer to Shopify: it checks a plan, names it by its SHA-256 and sends step i only while a person's approval stands (ADR-0023). All paths are in ovs-dlab5-net, under backend/amplify/."
      ]
    }
  ]
